{
  "id": "boss_drowned_reeve",
  "name": "The Drowned Reeve",
  "tier": "boss",
  "body": "ossuary_crawler",
  "place": "dungeon flooded_cistern set A: the end boss in the great cistern hall (28 m)",
  "_doc": "Stream E (M2). The town reeve who drowned closing the cistern gates during the great flood, still on duty. P1 \"Gate Duty\": a mace for the tank, chains thrown at random players, and FLOODWATER that rises in rings — the four sluice levers each drain one quarter of the room (repeatable). P2 at 60% \"Roll Call\": a ward of black water; he reads the names of the drowned (interruptible) and each name raises a drowned townsman; light the three signal lamps to break the ward. P3 new bar \"High Tide\": the whole floor floods except the raised plinths (safe circles), a three-player stack, a sweeping torrent, and the reeve's bell he rings for an enrage you must interrupt. Hard enrage 5.5 min.",
  "party": "Solo: very hard (levers + adds + interrupts); intended with a follower. 2-3: one tank, one lever/lamp runner. 5: as designed. M5: scale health x1.8 at 5, roll-call adds +1 per player, keep plinth count = party size + 1.",
